Grid lays children out in **two** directions at once.

```css title="gallery.css"
.gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  gap: 16px;
}
```

That single line makes a gallery that fits as many 180px-or-wider columns as the screen allows.

Draw the layout as text, then place children by name:

```css title="page.css"
.page {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas:
    "header header"
    "nav    main";
  grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
}
.page > nav { grid-area: nav; }
```
